  ! warning MR403 No lock_timeout before locking DDL

     ,- db/migrations/0002_fk.sql:1:1
   1 | ALTER TABLE orders ADD CONSTRAINT orders_user_id_f...
     | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^...
     |
     |- why     If a long query holds a lock on orders, this
     |          statement waits for it, and every query that
     |          arrives afterwards queues behind this
     |          statement.
     `- fix     Set a lock timeout at the top of the
                migration, and retry the migration if it
                times out:

                SET lock_timeout = '5s';

